- **Single source of truth** - Condition and message come only from config
- **Better separation of concerns** - Config data vs runtime event data
- **Maintained functionality** - All existing features still work

### ✅ **Client Usage Pattern:**
```rust
// Client receives AlarmEvent with just alarm_id
let alarm_event = AlarmEvent { alarm_id: "high_temp_alarm", ... };

// Client looks up details in config (which it already has)
let alarm_config = config.alarms.get(&alarm_event.alarm_id).unwrap();
let condition = &alarm_config.condition;
let message = &alarm_config.message;
```

All tests pass (54/54) and the example demonstrates the new structure working correctly. The change is backward compatible in terms of functionality while being more efficient for network communication.

